<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n15255" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">ef-flōresco</span></b> , rui, 3,
			<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>v. inch.
			n.</i>, <i>to bloom</i> or <i>blossom.</i>
		</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<b>Lit.</b> (eccl. Lat.),
				<i><span class="en">Vulg. Sirach, 51, 19</span></i>; <i><span class="en">id. Isa. 18,
				5</span></i>.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<b>Trop.</b> (repeatedly in Cic.), <i>to bloom</i>, <i>spring up</i>, <i>flourish</i> (in youth, beauty, etc.): 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">ex rerum cognitione efflorescat et redundet
					oportet oratio,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Cic.
					de Or. 1, 6, 20</span></i>
			; cf.: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">utilitas ex amicitia,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">id. Lael. 27</span></i>
			; so <i><span class="en">id. Rep. 1, 29</span></i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">amor,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">id.
					Fin. 1, 20, 69</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">si quidem efflorescit ingenii laudibus,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Cic.
					Cael. 31, 76</span></i>
			.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
